## Settled Direction

- Keep Codex as the operator interface and scripts as guarded state/projection machinery.
- Keep `work/100k.md` generated and read-only; do not add a second queue, database table, or
  lifecycle engine.
- Extend the existing executive-directive document contract with a concise human status capsule and
  checkbox milestones rather than attempting to infer human meaning from raw artifact counts.
- Derive checked state only from recorded evidence or reconciled subordinate outcomes; unchecked
  items make the remaining path visible.
- Group subordinate Ideas, maps, PRMs, campaigns, and outcomes beneath their owning directive and
  expose their IDs only for drill-down.
- Recommend one next move with its reason, blocker, required operator action, and safe alternative;
  never start it from a read-only view.
- Use owner-reviewed setup/migration to adopt existing strategy and lineage without continuous
  Markdown synchronization or duplicate authority.
- Preserve the completed 100k initiatives as history and record this work as a residual correction.

## Readiness Gate Transfer

1. `G1-DIRECTIVE-INTERACTION` — explicit and durable conversational directive lifecycle.
2. `G2-HUMAN-EXECUTIVE-ROLLUP` — human first screen and evidence-backed checkbox progress.
3. `G3-DISPLAYTEST-WORK2-DOGFOOD` — regression, hosted parity, and configured Work2 qualification.

## Program Shape

Use one bounded milestone and one campaign. Implement the smallest coherent contract across the
directive template, route guidance, projection, dashboard payload/template, documentation, and
focused tests. Commit the candidate, deploy it to the configured Linux and Windows development test
beds, verify the changed behavior with DisplayTest-centered fixtures or read-only evidence, register
the Work2 candidate and open owner chain, and stop before production release.

## Constraints And Non-Goals

- No production release, push, publication, or live DisplayTest mutation.
- No automatic execution from reading 100k.
- No continuous arbitrary strategy-Markdown authority.
- No fabricated checkbox completion from lifecycle labels alone.
- No replacement of existing Ideas, roadmaps, campaigns, outcomes, or planning order.

## Completion Boundary

Complete when the three transferred gates pass in one committed Work2 candidate, the changed
behavior is verified on both configured development lanes, and the candidate plus open IDEA-0033
ownership chain is registered without claiming production release.

